@@ -67,6 +67,28 @@ ## User Administration
 
 ## Queue and Tickets
 
+### Queue lifecycle and access
+
+Queues are created, renamed and deactivated only by **owner/admin** of the entity
+(`App\\Actions\\CreateQueue`, `App\\Actions\\UpdateQueue`). Name is trimmed and
+1–255 chars; slug defaults to `Str::slug(name)` and is unique within the
+entity. There is **no hard delete**: a queue is retired by setting
+`is_active = false`, which preserves its tickets; issuing or calling on an
+inactive queue raises `InactiveQueueException`.
+
+Per-queue access grants live in `queue_access` (join between
+`entity_memberships` and `queues`). A manager sets a membership's permissions
+on a queue via `App\\Actions\\SetQueueAccess`: a non-empty list upserts the
+row, an empty list revokes it. The only permission today is `call`
+(`App\\Enums\\QueuePermission::Call`). Audit entries `queue.access.granted` /
+`queue.access.revoked` are written to the `audit` channel.
+
+Authorization is centralized in `App\\Policies\\QueuePolicy`:
+`create`/`update`/`manageAccess` require owner/admin of the queue's entity;
+`call` allows owner/admin always and an employee only with a `queue_access`
+row for that queue whose `permissions` contains `call`. Both `CallNextTicket`
+and `Ticket::call()` enforce `call`.
+
 ### Ticket
 
 Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `status`, `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` (filled when called). Attributes:
